<div class="live-badge"><div class="live-dot"></div>2026 FIFA World Cup — USA in the Round of 16 · vs Belgium July 6</div>
<h1>USMNT <em>Speed &amp; Athletic Profiles</em></h1>
<div class="hero-meta">
<span class="hero-meta-item">📅 June 27, 2026</span>
<span class="hero-meta-item">🇺🇸 Team USA · 2026 World Cup</span>
<span class="hero-meta-item">📊 Athletic Breakdown</span>
</div>
<p class="hero-intro">
    Christian Pulisic and Folarin Balogun are both 5 feet 10 inches tall and weigh 161 pounds. They are the two most dangerous American players at the 2026 World Cup. Here is the full breakdown of their speed, athleticism, and physical profiles — and how the USA stacks up physically against the tournament's elite.
  </p>
</div><div class="article-wrap">
<div class="content">
<h2>Team USA at the 2026 World Cup — Group Stage Results</h2>
<div class="results-strip">
<div class="result-item">
<div class="result-score win">4–1</div>
<div class="result-opp">vs Paraguay</div>
<div class="result-note">Balogun 2 goals · June 12</div>
</div>
<div class="result-item">
<div class="result-score win">2–0</div>
<div class="result-opp">vs Australia</div>
<div class="result-note">Balogun forced own goal · June 19</div>
</div>
<div class="result-item">
<div class="result-score win">2–0</div>
<div class="result-opp">vs Bosnia (R32)</div>
<div class="result-note">Balogun goal &amp; red card · July 1</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>The United States won Group D, beat Bosnia and Herzegovina 2-0 in the Round of 32, and are now in the Round of 16 against Belgium on Monday July 6 at Lumen Field in Seattle. <strong>Balogun scored the opening goal against Bosnia in the 45th minute</strong> before being sent off in the 64th minute for stepping on an opponent's leg. The step appeared accidental — he was looking ahead and slightly off-balance — but slow-motion replays prompted referee Raphael Claus to show a red card, and an automatic one-game suspension means <strong>Balogun misses the Belgium match</strong>. Malik Tillman added the second goal in the 82nd minute. Pulisic now carries the attack for the most important game in USMNT history.</p>
<div class="callout">
<div class="callout-icon">🟥</div>
<div class="callout-text"><strong>Balogun suspended for USA vs Belgium:</strong> Four goals and three goal contributions across the tournament. Red-carded in the 64th minute of USA's biggest win. The player who carried the American attack through the group stage will watch from the stands Monday in Seattle while Pulisic, McKennie, and Tillman face the 2026 semifinalist Belgians without him. The physical profile that made him so dangerous — the shot power, the first-step burst, the low center of gravity — won't be on the pitch for 90 minutes that could define this generation of American soccer.</div>
</div>
<h2>Folarin Balogun — The Breakout Star</h2>
<div class="player-card usa">
<div class="player-name">Folarin Balogun</div>
<div class="player-sub">USMNT · Striker · AS Monaco · Age 24 · Born Brooklyn, NY</div>
<div class="player-stats">
<div class="pstat">
<div class="pstat-val">5'10"</div>
<div class="pstat-lbl">Height</div>
</div>
<div class="pstat">
<div class="pstat-val">161 lb</div>
<div class="pstat-lbl">Weight</div>
</div>
<div class="pstat">
<div class="pstat-val">2</div>
<div class="pstat-lbl">Goals (group stage)</div>
</div>
<div class="pstat">
<div class="pstat-val">3</div>
<div class="pstat-lbl">Goal contributions</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Balogun's group stage was extraordinary by any measure. Two goals against Paraguay in the opener — the first a sharp one-touch finish, the second a powerful drive into the upper corner after fighting through the defense — made him the first American to score twice in a single World Cup game since Bert Patenaude in 1930. His blistering run and low cross against Australia forced an own goal in the 11th minute, putting the USA ahead before anyone in Seattle had finished their drinks.</p>
<p>What makes Balogun's athletic profile interesting for this site is the combination of measurements. At 5'10" and 161 pounds, he is smaller than most elite center-forwards — Haaland at 6'4" and 194 pounds outweighs him by 33 pounds and is 6 inches taller. But Balogun's power-to-weight ratio produces the heavy shot his own goalkeeper tapes his thumbs to face in practice, and his acceleration off the shoulder of the last defender is what generates his scoring opportunities rather than superior size.</p>
<div class="callout">
<div class="callout-icon">🇺🇸</div>
<div class="callout-text"><strong>The Brooklyn-born, London-raised, American striker story:</strong> Balogun's mother was visiting New York when she was seven months pregnant and was not allowed to board the return flight home to London. He was born in Brooklyn, moved to London two months later, grew up there, came through Arsenal's academy, and in 2023 chose to represent the United States over England and Nigeria. He is now the most important striker in the history of the USMNT program. The geographic accident of his birth has produced the most consequential coincidence in American soccer.</div>
</div>
<h3>How Fast Is Balogun?</h3>
<p>Balogun's specific tracked top speed at the 2026 World Cup has not been officially published, but FIFA tracking data from his club season and World Cup performances puts his top-end speed at approximately 33 to 34 km/h — roughly 20.5 to 21.1 mph. This is solidly fast for a center-forward but well below the sprint specialists at the tournament.</p>
<p>What separates him athletically is not speed but <strong>explosive power generation</strong>. The shot strength that wraps his goalkeeper's thumbs in tape, the ability to fight through defenders and still deliver a strike on frame, and the first-step acceleration that lets him pin the last defender and attack the space behind them — these are power qualities rather than speed qualities, and they are harder to measure but more important for his position.</p>
<h2>Christian Pulisic — Captain America</h2>
<div class="player-card usa">
<div class="player-name">Christian Pulisic</div>
<div class="player-sub">USMNT Captain · Right Winger · AC Milan · Age 27 · Hershey, PA</div>
<div class="player-stats">
<div class="pstat">
<div class="pstat-val">5'10"</div>
<div class="pstat-lbl">Height</div>
</div>
<div class="pstat">
<div class="pstat-val">161 lb</div>
<div class="pstat-lbl">Weight</div>
</div>
<div class="pstat">
<div class="pstat-val">~21.7</div>
<div class="pstat-lbl">Top speed (mph)</div>
</div>
<div class="pstat">
<div class="pstat-val">27</div>
<div class="pstat-lbl">Age</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Pulisic's World Cup was complicated by a calf injury sustained in the first game against Paraguay that kept him out of the Australia match and limited him to substitute appearances. He returned against Türkiye as the group stage concluded. At full fitness, he is the most dangerous dribbling threat on the USA roster and the player opposing defenders plan their defensive shape around.</p>
<p>His recorded top speed of approximately 34 to 35 km/h (21.1 to 21.7 mph) is fast for a winger but not elite by 2026 World Cup standards — Mbappé at 38 km/h and van de Ven at 37.38 km/h both significantly exceed it. What Pulisic produces is first-step quickness from a standing position, the ability to accelerate into the channel before defenders can recover their shape, and a dribbling style built around rapid change of direction rather than outrunning defenders in a straight line.</p>
