<p>The table reveals something striking: <strong>Pulisic is almost identical physically to Mbappé</strong> — same height, one pound heavier, same age. The gap between them is not physical. Mbappé at 23.6 mph career best is roughly 2 mph faster than Pulisic. That speed gap is real, but the primary difference between the two players is the volume and quality of the goalscoring production Mbappé has accumulated across a decade of elite club football.</p>
<p>Balogun at 5'10" and 161 pounds is also physically similar to Viniúcius Jr. — who plays wide rather than central, but at comparable size. The USA's two best players sit in the middle of the tournament's physical range — neither the imposing size of Haaland nor the slight build of Lamine Yamal. They are physically unremarkable by the standards of the elite players they are competing with. Their output is not.</p>
